# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keystatic CMS
#
# For local development: leave ALL of these empty. The CMS then edits the files in
# your working tree directly, with no login. Nothing here is needed to run the site.
#
# For the team: you only fill in the FIRST variable by hand. Keystatic generates the
# other four and writes them into .env for you — see docs/07-cms-setup.md for the
# click-by-click walkthrough.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. YOU SET THIS ONE.
#    The GitHub repository the CMS commits content to, written as "owner/name" —
#    exactly what comes after github.com/ in the repo's address.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_REPO=

# 2-5. KEYSTATIC WRITES THESE FOR YOU.
#      With the variable above set, run the site locally and open /keystatic. It shows a
#      setup screen, you click through to GitHub once, and on the way back it appends
#      these four lines to your .env file. You then copy them into your host.
#
#        APP_SLUG      the name GitHub gave your app, used to build the sign-in link
#        CLIENT_ID     the app's public identifier with GitHub
#        CLIENT_SECRET the app's password with GitHub — never commit or share this
#        SECRET        a random key this site uses to sign editors' login cookies
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
KEYSTATIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
KEYSTATIC_SECRET=
